Deathtrap Native 50 @VERSION@
================================

Free unofficial modernization patch for the 32-bit Steam release of
Ian Livingstone's Deathtrap Dungeon (1998).

Developed using OpenAI Codex under human direction and validated through
extensive manual playtesting and automated tests.

Tested game:
https://store.steampowered.com/app/245010/Deathtrap_Dungeon/

Gameplay demo:
https://youtu.be/U1RjdVP49TQ

The complete user-facing list of changes is included in CHANGELOG.txt.

QUICK INSTALL

Everything required for the supported setup is already included. You do not
need to download or configure dgVoodoo before the first launch.

1. Close the game.
2. Extract every file from this patch ZIP directly beside DD_CD.EXE. Preserve
   the included payload directory.
3. Double-click INSTALL.cmd once.
4. Start Deathtrap Dungeon normally through Steam or DD_CD.EXE.

INSTALL.cmd backs up any existing patch, dgVoodoo, control and rendering files,
then installs the complete tested setup. The archive includes the tested
Deathtrap Dd7to9 native-canvas layer and unmodified dgVoodoo 2.86.2 x86 D3D9
backend. It uses D3D11 FL11 with an aspect-correct canvas (1800 pixels high at
the default internal scale of 3), 8x MSAA, 16x texture filtering, automatic
mipmaps and VSync. dgVoodoo resolution remains unforced so the canvas is never
scaled a second time.

DISPLAY MODE AND WINDOW SIZE

The installer detects the current primary monitor in physical pixels and
writes that size to deathtrap_native.ini. The default mode is a desktop-sized
borderless window with no exclusive-fullscreen resolution switch:

[Display]
Mode=borderless
WindowWidth=2880
WindowHeight=1800

The dimensions above are an example; the installed values match the machine
on which INSTALL.cmd runs. Borderless always fills the current monitor.

For a normal centered framed window, change Mode to windowed and set the exact
client size you want, for example:

[Display]
Mode=windowed
WindowWidth=1280
WindowHeight=720

Restart the game after changing display settings.

OPTIONAL DGVOODOO TUNING

No tuning is required to run the patch. Display mode and window size are owned
by deathtrap_native.ini. To inspect or change advanced wrapper options such as
antialiasing or texture filtering, download the complete official dgVoodoo
package from:

https://github.com/dege-diosg/dgVoodoo2/releases

Copy only dgVoodooCpl.exe beside DD_CD.EXE and the installed dgVoodoo.conf,
then run it and apply your preferred settings to the game directory. The
required x86 runtime DLLs are already installed by this patch. Do not replace
them with x64 wrappers. Keep the General tab set to Windowed, DirectX
resolution set to Unforced, and OutputAPI set to d3d11_fl11_0.

For lower-end systems, reduce Antialiasing (MSAA) to 4x or 2x; do not apply a
dgVoodoo resolution multiplier. Reference screenshots are included as
optional\dgVoodoo-General.png and
optional\dgVoodoo-DirectX.png.

The tested Steam Dungeon.dll SHA-256 is:
95FE9CE0FFF387F00704548F152E4340815213FCB3833DBE1B5C42871E7D2E56

The tested Steam DD_CD.EXE SHA-256 is:
0C644A00E62652E046C5DAD2960F0F6C8C1998F4CA065780FBD7811D9908BF1F

The installer warns but continues if the game hashes differ. Untested game
files may be partially or completely incompatible.

MOUSE AND KEYBOARD

Mouse movement     Rotate modern camera / first-person look
Left mouse         Attack; A/D choose a side and S selects the turning attack
Right mouse        Block or parry
Mouse wheel        Previous/next available melee weapon
W / S              Walk forward/backward
Shift + W / S      Run forward/backward
A / D              Turn left/right
Shift + A / D      Fast turn left/right
J / K              Side-step left/right
Ctrl + W / S       Step forward/backward
Ctrl + A / D       Original side-step left/right
Space              Jump or climb
Space + direction  Directional jump
F                  Ranged attack / original combat modifier
F + W/A/D          Original directional melee attacks
F + S              Original parry
Q                  Cast/use selected spell
E                  Operate or interact
F1 / F2 / F3 / F4 Melee / ranged / spell-shield / consumable selector
1-8                Choose slot in an opened retail item selector
Tab                Original retail first-person view
F10                Body-visible immersive first-person view
F11                Toggle approximately 50 FPS native presentation
P                  Pause gameplay
Esc                Open or leave menu; save and load through the retail menu

Immersive first person uses A/D for pure full-speed side movement. Combine
W/S with A/D for diagonals and hold Shift to run.

F1-F4 selectors slow the game world to 25% by default while camera and input
remain full-rate. Change SlowMotionPercent under [Selector] in
deathtrap_native.ini if desired.

Keyboard Setup has two pages for all twenty actions. Use << and >> on the
right to switch pages. Keyboard Default restores the complete modern profile.
Keyboard changes never alter the fixed controller layout.

The patch enables the retail Save command at safe grounded positions outside
the original save points. Saving and loading still use the original menu,
slot screens and save-file format.

XBOX-COMPATIBLE CONTROLLER

Left stick         Camera-relative movement; full tilt runs / menu navigation
Right stick        Camera or first-person look / menu pointer / radial choice
A                  Jump or climb / confirm / skip supported screens
B                  Back in menus
X                  Operate or interact / alternate screen skip
Y                  Unassigned
RT                 Attack; left stick selects directional attacks
LT                 Block or parry
RB                 Cast/use contextual spell action
LB + left stick    Original side-step movement
Start/Menu         Open pause menu / leave menu
R3                 Original retail first-person view
L3                 Body-visible immersive first-person view
View/Back          Pause/resume gameplay
D-pad tap          Cycle next item in the selected category
D-pad hold         Open radial selector; choose with right stick

D-pad categories: up melee, right ranged, down spells/shields, left
potions/charms.

PROJECTS AND REPOSITORIES USED

MinHook 1.3.4 - statically linked API-hooking dependency:
https://github.com/TsudaKageyu/minhook

dxwrapper - bundled Deathtrap-specific Dd7to9 layer:
https://github.com/elishacloud/dxwrapper

dgVoodoo2 - bundled D3D9/D3DImm runtime:
https://github.com/dege-diosg/dgVoodoo2

Unity Cinemachine - camera design reference; no code included:
https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/com.unity.cinemachine

UE Explorer - Arkham Asylum camera research tool; no code included:
https://github.com/UE-Explorer/UE-Explorer

ogg-winmm - Steam music-routing research reference; not included or required:
https://github.com/bangstk/ogg-winmm

ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS

Thanks to the community members who helped test public builds:

- dbdk422a
- 517342 - for testing and identifying the directional-control problems
  fixed in version 0.0.221

The installer creates a timestamped backup of existing patch files,
DDraw.dll, dxwrapper.dll, D3D9.dll, D3DImm.dll, both wrapper configurations,
ASYLUM\keys.cfg and ASYLUM\config.dat
under the game's back directory before applying the verified setup. It then
installs the exact keys.cfg shipped with this DLL; do not copy a control file
from another installation over it.

HELP AND BUG REPORTS

Discord #help-and-bug-reports:
https://discord.gg/9tP8qFG7Y

SUPPORT LOG

Every launch automatically creates one compact timestamped file under the
game's logs directory. If a problem occurs, reproduce it once, close the game
and attach the newest deathtrap-native-*.log file to the report. The file
already contains the patch version, relevant display and dgVoodoo settings,
and a low-rate input/cursor summary. No diagnostic setting needs to be enabled.

This patch contains no game assets. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES must remain with
redistributed copies of the patch.

